  "name": "Seattle Kraken (2024)",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "B39M",
  "description": "Fuselage: Forward fuselage standard Alaska white; from over the wing aft, forward-leaning bands of ice blue, cyan and deep-sea navy, the navy covering the aft fuselage. Cheatlines: A Kraken-red stripe in the navy, leaning the same way, from the crown to just below the windows; Alaska's cyan/lime swoosh near the tail. Tail: Standard Alaska midnight-blue fin with the Alaska Native man's face and lime/cyan stripes. Engines: White with the standard blue/green swoosh. Winglets: Standard. Titles: Standard midnight-blue 'Alaska' script forward with Seattle's coordinates in small type under it. Artwork: Large Seattle Kraken 'S' logo (ice blue and cyan with a red eye) on the navy behind the wing. Colors hex: Kraken team colors (Deep Sea Blue #001628, Ice Blue #99D9D9, Red Alert #E9072B) are team-published; the paint here is matched by eye.",
  "sources": [
